# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<template>
  <input ref="input" />
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
import { ref } from "vue";

const input = ref<HTMLInputElement | null>(null);
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-typescript.vue:9:7 lint/nursery/useVueTemplateRef ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i The template ref input is created with ref().
  
     7 │ import { ref } from "vue";
     8 │ 
   > 9 │ const input = ref<HTMLInputElement | null>(null);
       │       ^^^^^
    10 │ </script>
    11 │ 
  
  i Vue links this variable to the element only by its name, so renaming the variable breaks the link without warning.
  
  i Use useTemplateRef("input") instead, which names the element explicitly.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

